      <div class="eb-bio-copy">
        <div class="eb-label">The Long Version</div>
        <h2 class="eb-h2">Hi, I'm Eshun.</h2>

        <p>I'm from Sarasota, Florida. I love to spend my time competing in STEM competitions, building websites, and traveling the world.</p>

        <p>As an <strong>International Baccalaureate Diploma Programme</strong> student at Southeast High School, I'm interested in computer science, engineering, and technology. Throughout middle and high school, my experience has centered around STEM through leadership, competition, and research. I'm actively involved in numerous organizations including the Technology Student Association, HOSA Future Health Professionals, National STEM Honor Society, and varsity swimming.</p>

        <p>I served as the <strong>2025–2026 Florida TSA State Reporter</strong> and was elected to serve as the <strong>2026–2027 Florida TSA State Secretary</strong>. Through TSA I've competed at the district, state, and national levels, earning awards in website design, software development, public speaking, and graphic design.</p>

        <p>In addition to leadership and competition, I participate in the <strong>Southeast High School Research Program</strong>, where I conduct independent STEM research and compete in science and engineering fairs. My research has advanced to the State Science and Engineering Fair and has received state-level recognition. Outside of research, I stay involved in STEM outreach and mentorship opportunities that support younger students entering technical and competitive programs.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

